\description{
Direct data.table dispatch: the in-memory caller (e.g. GiottoClass's
\code{createNetwork()} machinery) hands a pre-canonicalized edge data.table with
character \code{from} / \code{to} columns plus optional \code{weight} / \code{distance} /
\code{shared}. Trusts the caller for canonical form — no swap, no dedup.

igraph dispatch: extracts edges via \code{igraph::as_data_frame()} and the
vertex universe via \code{V(g)$name}, then delegates to the data.table
path. Directedness defaults to \code{igraph::is_directed(data)} if not
explicitly passed. Used by GiottoClass's network setters when a
giotto object has a gsource backend.

Write data to a \code{dataStore} inheriting class (usually a subclass of
\link[=fileStore-class]{fileStore}). This documentation covers the basic expected API.
